{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefectClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefectClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.pieceA_hook_content_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.pieceA_hook_content_identity","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L210-L228","doc":"**Piece A — the per-partition hook–content identity** (HLF-free):\n`Σ_{c∈λ} h_c² = Σ_{c∈λ} content(c)² + n²`, where `n = Σλ`. This is the `2n²`\npiece of Identity I's content decomposition (`twoM_content_decomposition`),\nsummed under the Plancherel measure via `E_Planch[n²] = n²`.\n\n**Why this matters for Identity I.** Piece A uses **no** hook-length formula, no\n`dim`, no SYT count, no RSK — it is a single-Young-diagram combinatorial fact\n(`sumHookSq` vs `sumContentSq`, no `dimOf`). Verified here for every partition of\n`n = 1..8` (and `n = 0`, vacuously) — extended 2026-08-01 to cover the\nphysically-critical `n = 7` defect sign-flip. General `n`: **proved sorry-free** in\n[`QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.pieceA`](PieceAGeneral.lean) over Mathlib's `YoungDiagram`\n(bean `qou-o5xj` closed) — an explicit elementary, HLF-free, dimension-free\ndouble-counting proof (Piece A reduces to `Σ_c arm·leg + Σ_c above·left = D`, the\noff-diagonal pair count). The `List ℕ` `decide` checks here (`n ≤ 8`) are a\nconcrete cross-check of the same identity in this file's representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM_eq_numer_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM_eq_numer_base","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L203-L208","doc":"**Consistency with the carried `twoM`.** `twoM n = n(3n−1) = 2·M(n)`; at the\nverified `n` this matches the computed numerator: `twoM n · n! = 2·numerComputed n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.identityI_computed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.identityI_computed","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L188-L201","doc":"**Identity I — verified for `n = 1..8`.** `M(n) = n(3n−1)/2`, in cleared form\n`2·numerComputed n = n(3n−1)·n!` (RHS `n(3n−1)`: 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17, 20, 23).\nComputed from hooks/`dim`, not hand-tabulated — dodge-proof. Extended to `n = 7, 8`\n(2026-08-01) to cover the physically-critical `n = 7` defect sign-flip region. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.numerComputed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.numerComputed","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L184-L186","doc":"`Σ_{λ⊢n} dim(λ)² · Σ_{c∈λ} h_c²` — computed from the partition structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.partitionsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.partitionsOf","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L164-L182","doc":"The partitions of `n`, supplied as explicit descending lists (the\ncombinatorial content — hooks, `dim`, the sum — is computed, not tabulated). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sumContentSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sumContentSq","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L161-L162","doc":"`Σ_{c∈λ} content(c)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.contents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.contents","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L154-L159","doc":"Content `c(cell) = j − i` of each cell, enumerated over the SAME cells as\n`hookLengths` (row `i`, column `j`). Structurally computable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sumHookSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sumHookSq","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L151-L152","doc":"`Σ_{c∈λ} h_c²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.dimOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.dimOf","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L147-L149","doc":"`dim λ = (Σλ)! / ∏ h_c` (hook-length formula). Exact ℕ division — the HLF\nguarantees `∏ h_c ∣ n!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.hookLengths","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.hookLengths","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L138-L145","doc":"Multiset of hook lengths of a partition `l` (descending row lengths). Cell\n`(i,j)` has hook `arm + leg + 1`, with `arm = l_i − 1 − j` (cells to the right)\nand `leg = #{i' > i : l_{i'} > j}` (cells below). Structurally computable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_neg","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L99-L105","doc":"**Negative regime.** `C(n) < 0` for `n ≥ 7` (all three factors positive, so\nthe negation is negative). This is the exact `n = 7` sign change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_pos","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L94-L97","doc":"**Positive regime.** `C(n) > 0` for `2 ≤ n ≤ 6` (the factor `2n−13 < 0`,\ntimes the positive `n(n−1)`, negated). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_table","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L87-L92","doc":"Table cross-check against #2525's empirical sequence `24·C(n) = 3, 7, 10, 10,\n5, −7, −28` for `n = 2..8` (so `144·C(n) = 6·` that). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**Closed form (the keystone result).** Given Identity I, the defect\ncoefficient is the cubic `144·C(n) = −n(n−1)(2n−13)`. Pure ring identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.n144C","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L77-L79","doc":"`144·C(n)`. From `24·C(n) = 2·M(n) − S_n − 2n`, clearing denominators by `6`\ngives `144·C(n) = 6·(2M(n)) − 6·S_n − 12n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sixS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.sixS","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L73-L75","doc":"`6·S_n`, where `S_n = Σ_{k=1}^n (k²−1) = n(n+1)(2n+1)/6 − n`. Cleared of the\n`/6` to stay in `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM_content_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM_content_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L53-L71","doc":"**Identity I, content decomposition.** `2·M(n)` splits into the two carried\npieces (cf. `docs/audits/2026-06-23-keystone-identity-I-content-decomposition.md`),\neach attributed and *neither using the Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook-length formula*:\n\n* `n·(n−1) = 2·binom(n,2) = 2·E_Planch[Σ_c c(c)²]` — piece **B**, the standard\n  Jucys–Murphy / Plancherel content-square mean (central `Σ_k X_k²`, identity\n  coefficient `Σ_{k=1}^n (k−1) = binom(n,2)`);\n* `2·n²` — piece **A**, the per-partition hook-content identity\n  `Σ_c h_c² = Σ_c c(c)² + n²` (a single-Young-diagram fact, no dimensions) summed\n  under the Plancherel measure (`E_Planch[n²] = n²`).\n\nThis makes Identity I transparent, and both pieces are now proved sorry-free:\n(A) `QOU.BraidKnot.PieceA.pieceA` (`PieceAGeneral.lean`, general-`n`, HLF-free\ncell-pair double-counting) and (B) `identityB_via_wedderburn_unconditional`\n(`IdentityBWedderburn.lean`, the `ℂ[S_n]` JM/Wedderburn content-square mean). Pure\n`ℤ` ring identity (`n(n−1)+2n² = 3n²−n = n(3n−1)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WLambdaDefect.twoM","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WLambdaDefectClosedForm.lean#L45-L51","doc":"`2·M(n)`, where `M(n) = n(3n−1)/2` is the Plancherel-expected squared-hook sum\n(**Identity I**). Identity I is a sorry-free general-`n` theorem\n(`PlancherelSnDataGeneral.two_sum_dim_sq_hooks_general`,\n`twoM_eq_plancherel_hook_sum_general`); this `twoM` is its cleared-`½` `ℤ` shadow.\nContent-decomposed in\n`docs/audits/2026-06-23-keystone-identity-I-content-decomposition.md`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}